{
 "_about": "THE TELLY IN VITAL PLANT LIVING, Ryan's brief, 2026-10-01: the last month of videos, shorts included, from plant-based cooks he chose, refilled every morning with the older ones going off the end. The cooks are his, in his order; the videos are not chosen one by one, and the room says nobody here watched them first. tools/pull-vital-rack.py reads each channel's own two feeds (UULF, its long-form uploads, and UUSH, its shorts) and asks each new video's watch page once, the morning it arrives; tools/make-vital.py draws the telly from this file; tools/daily-vital.sh runs both on the morning timer and commits only this file and vital-plant-living.html. This file is the timer's: hand-edit `sources` on purpose and nothing else.",
 "_sources": "Each channel id was read off the channel's own page on 2026-10-01 (its externalId), never typed from memory. `name` is the channel's own name as YouTube gives it, with a typographic apostrophe; `url` is the channel's front page without the tab Ryan's link happened to be on. A new cook is a new entry here with its id read the same way; the puller derives both feeds from the id.",
 "_window": "A MONTH IS THIRTY DAYS, counted back from the minute the telly was filled. A video published before that goes off the end on the next fill; make-vital.py refuses a file still holding one, because a rack that keeps everything is an archive, and the brief was the last month.",
 "_telly": "A VIDEO IS AN ID, A TITLE, A CHANNEL, A TIME AND A LENGTH, the Doom Scoop's rule: no description, no thumbnail, no count of views, likes or subscribers, and make-vital.py refuses a row carrying any of them. `form` is long or short, by which of the channel's two feeds carried it; a short plays upright. `state` is what its watch page said: screen (plays here), door (plays on YouTube only: embedding off, or age-gated), pending (live, or not out yet, asked again tomorrow) or gone (not drawn). TITLES ARE QUOTED AS WRITTEN, capitals, emoji and all, and the room's sweeps skip them: they are the cooks' words, and a title about protein or bodies is theirs to write, beside a house rule of ours that says nobody in here tells you what a bowl does for your body.",
 "_covered": "What the feeds have been read all the way through, per channel and per feed. A YouTube feed carries the latest fifteen and a busy channel puts up more than that in a month; a channel whose coverage does not reach back to the start of the month says so on the page. Generated, never typed.",
